---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Bags on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet: 2026 lane guide (totes, crossbody, freight) | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="A data-backed guide to bags and leather-goods rows on kakobuy-cn.com—14 backpack-lane cards plus cross-lane context, brand clusters from Goyard to Coach, and branded shipping reality before you paste into Kakobuy."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Bags lane guide: totes, crossbody, and leather goods on the Kakobuy Spreadsheet (2026)"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="9 June 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'Kakobuy Spreadsheet bags',
    'Goyard Louis Vuitton reps bag guide',
    'leather goods agent shipping 2026',
    'crossbody tote spreadsheet',
    'kakobuy-cn.com bags lane',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Bags look like the easiest spreadsheet rows—one photo, one price—until customs asks about leather logos and your freight line rejects branded leather entirely.
    This guide maps the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> bag lanes as of <strong>9 June 2026</strong>: <strong>14 rows</strong> in the deep <code>bags-backpacks</code> pool behind the homepage <a href="/category/bags/">Bags</a> shortcut, plus how adjacent accessory lanes overlap when you search by brand instead of category.
  </p>

  <h2>June 2026 bags snapshot</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Bags lane</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Deep-lane rows (<code>bags-backpacks</code>)</td><td>14</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Top labels (2–3 rows each)</td><td>Coach, Dior, Goyard, Louis Vuitton</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Also indexed</td><td>Burberry, Gucci</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Homepage shortcut</td><td><a href="/category/bags/">Bags</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Counts come from our on-site English catalogue export. Brand strings describe seller metadata—not authorised distribution.
    Wallets and card holders often live in <a href="/category/accessories/">Accessories</a> or belt lanes; search by brand if a tote row is missing.
  </p>

  <h2>What shoppers actually browse</h2>
  <h3>Monogram &amp; woven classics (Goyard, Louis Vuitton)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Goyard</strong> Saint Louis–style totes and <strong>Louis Vuitton</strong> monogram crossbody rows dominate our snapshot.
    QC focus: canvas alignment, handle attachment, interior stamp clarity, hardware weight.
    These SKUs trigger <a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">branded shipping</a> scrutiny—confirm route eligibility before you build a bag-only cart.
  </p>
  <h3>Designer leather (Dior, Gucci, Burberry)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Dior</strong> book totes and saddle-adjacent silhouettes appear repeatedly; <strong>Gucci</strong> and <strong>Burberry</strong> show less often but still index.
    Compare stitching rhythm and logo placement in warehouse stills—seller studio lighting hides emboss depth.
  </p>
  <h3>Accessible luxury (Coach)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Coach</strong> rows price lower in ¥ than European houses but still carry trademark strings.
    Do not assume “affordable row” equals unbranded postal lines.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist for bag rows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Hardware:</strong> zipper pull branding, buckle engravings, clasp alignment.</li>
    <li><strong>Canvas/leather panels:</strong> pattern continuity across seams.</li>
    <li><strong>Interior:</strong> lining colour, pocket layout, stamp fonts.</li>
    <li><strong>Structure:</strong> base feet, handle glazing, strap edge paint.</li>
    <li><strong>Included pouches:</strong> verify presence if listing promises matching clutch.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Deep-read <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">warehouse QC</a> and <a href="/blog/kakobuy-4k-qc-video-inspection-guide/">4K video</a> for curved panels bags need.
  </p>

  <h2>Freight &amp; consolidation notes</h2>
  <p>
    Bags are rarely volumetric monsters compared to parkas, but boxy totes still bill DIM weight if shipped in oversized seller packaging.
    Consolidate with apparel using <a href="/blog/kakobuy-rehearsal-packaging-freight/">rehearsal packaging</a> when near a freight bracket edge.
    Budget with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-first-haul-budget-planner-2026/">first haul templates</a> if this is your opening cart.
  </p>

  <h2>Browse workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet home</a></strong> → <a href="/category/bags/">Bags</a>.</li>
    <li>Copy live marketplace URLs—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">URL hygiene</a>.</li>
    <li>Paste into Kakobuy; freeze colour/size variants.</li>
    <li>Approve QC on hardware and monogram alignment.</li>
    <li>Quote branded-safe outbound lines before you pay freight.</li>
  </ol>
